>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `quickcheck`

``` hol4
Refute.quickcheck : term -> outcome
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runs Refute's executable Quickcheck backends.

`Refute.quickcheck tm` calls `Refute.refute` using `!Refute.the_config`
after forcing backend selection to `SOME ["exhaustive", "random"]`.
Every other field of the current configuration is preserved, including
substrate, size, iterations, seed, smart-generator options, certification,
quiet mode, and expectations.

The exhaustive and random backends use the `Auto`, `NativeSML`, `Cv`, or
`Compute` substrate selected by the configuration.  Narrowing is a
separate backend and is not selected by this convenience entry point.

